    "basis": "reconstruction",
    "fidelity": "not-applicable",
    "note": "The finished design was read from Wichmann’s SPA0807 drawing, an interlace of bands, by their centre lines. Its corners were snapped to the square-root-of-two grid in star-radius units, in the tile’s four directions and in the four directions turned by 22.5°. The tile’s half side is (1 + √2)² star radii: line OS2 meets the vertical through A at height 1 + √2, and line OS1 carries that out to the tile’s side. One helper line, the horizontal through P, is not in the finished pattern. The drawing gives no steps; we devised the construction.",
    "changes": "The compass steps, their order and the named points are ours. The lines are the centre lines of the drawing’s bands; the over-and-under weave is drawn by the player’s interlace look. Laid over Wade’s photo SPA 0807, our lines follow the square frames and the corner stars on the flat jamb; the turned stars lie where the wall curves into the arch, so the photo could not confirm or correct them, and the drawing is kept.",
    "reviewed": "2026-10-26"
  },
